<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Cherasco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1631</span> · Also known as Peace of Cherasco · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-mantuan-succession">War of the Mantuan Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Cherasco, signed in 1631 at Cherasco in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-mantuan-succession">War of the Mantuan Succession</a>. It confirmed the French-backed Charles I Gonzaga-Nevers as Duke of Mantua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, while Savoy received part of Montferrat, including Alba and Trino. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> secretly kept the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinerolo">Pinerolo</a>, which gave it a gateway into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div>
